            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "value": "The obvious fix — prune unconditionally on a timer — would steal samples from a real Prometheus between its scrapes, quietly lowering the counts it sees. So "
              },
              {
                "type": "code",
                "value": "MetricsController.scrape/2"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "value": " now reports each external scrape via "
              },
              {
                "type": "code",
                "value": "note_scrape/0"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "value": "… "
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "value": "An instance with Prometheus attached never sees this process do anything."
                  }
                ],
                "type": "strong"
              }
            ],
            "title": "He wrote",
            "tone": "success",
            "type": "callout"
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "value": "Core folds raw rows into cumulative histogram buckets, so an internal scrape does not steal already-counted samples. The idle window instead avoids redundant exposition work while a real Prometheus is attached…"
              }
            ],
            "title": "It was replaced with",
            "tone": "danger",
            "type": "callout"
          }
        ]
